# App Review demo account for scripts/review_account.sh (skill heji-review-account). Sourced as bash.
# The password is never here: it lives in ~/Credentials/review-accounts.env and App Store Connect.

REVIEW_EMAIL="appreview+headway@hejitech.com"
# The Worker that serves POST /api/review-sign-in, and where it runs.
WORKER_DIR="projects/headway/services/web"
WRANGLER_ENV="production"
SITE="https://headway.hejitech.workers.dev"
BUNDLE_ID="com.hejitech.headway"

# App Store Connect › App Review Information › Notes.
REVIEW_NOTES="Sign in: on the first screen tap \"Sign in with email\" (below Continue with Google) and use the demo account above. People create accounts with Sign in with Apple or Google; email sign-in is only for accounts we hand out, such as this one. Each sign-in with it starts from a demo commute (Mountain View to San Francisco in the morning, back in the evening).

What to try: Trains shows live Caltrain departures with leave-by times; swipe a train to track it (Live Activity on the Lock Screen). The ... menu pins the next trains to the Lock Screen. Home Screen widget: Next trains. Commute sets the legs and alerts. Location (Settings) is optional and only estimates the walk or drive to the station; it's never stored.

Family: the Family tab creates a group (up to 8 people) that the owner invites to by email; the invitee accepts in the app. Nothing is shared until each person turns on a share (their tracked train, their usual train running late, or a status) and picks who sees it. Seeing a shared train needs a second Headway account in the group, so the demo account starts with no group.

Settings > Even G2 Glasses pairs Even Realities G2 smart glasses with a 6-digit code; it needs the glasses and isn't required to use the app. The Apple Watch app shows the same board.

Account deletion: Settings > Delete my Headway data deletes the account and everything Headway keeps about it (commute, devices, assistant access, history) and signs out. The same sign-in also opens our other apps, so their data isn't touched."
